n citation-type="journal">Bustin, M., L. Trieschmann, and Y.V. Postnikov. <year>1995</year>. The HMG-14/-17 chromosomal protein family: architectural elements that enhance transcription from chromatin templates. <source>Semin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>247</fpage>&#x02013;255.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8562917</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Carbone, R., M. Pearson, S. Minucci, and P.G. Pelicci. <year>2002</year>. PML NBs associate with the hMre11 complex and p53 at sites of irradiation induced DNA damage. <source>Oncogene.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>1633</fpage>&#x02013;1640.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11896594</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Caron, H., B. van Schaik, M. van der Mee, F. Baas, G. Riggins, P. van Sluis, M.C. Hermus, R. van Asperen, K. Boon, P.A. Voute, et al. <year>2001</year>. The human transcriptome map: clustering of highly expressed genes in chromosomal domains. <source>Science.</source> <volume>291</volume>:<fpage>1289</fpage>&#x02013;1292.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11181992</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Carrel, L., A.A. Cottle, K.C. Goglin, and H.F. Willard. <year>1999</year>. A first-generation X-inactivation profile of the human X chromosome. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>14440</fpage>&#x02013;14444.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10588724</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Chubb, J.R., S. Boyle, P. Perry, and W.A. Bickmore. <year>2002</year>. Chromatin motion is constrained by association with nuclear compartments in human cells. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>439</fpage>&#x02013;445.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11909528</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Cremer, T., and C. Cremer. <year>2001</year>. Chromosome territories, nuclear architecture and